    deck: "Food and drink",
    body: `
<p>Food is at the center of Filipino visits, and the first questions you hear are about eating, not about how you are.</p>
<h3>Eating together</h3>
<p>English asks "How are you?"; Filipinos often ask "Have you eaten?" It is a friendly greeting, not an invitation you must accept. When someone starts eating, they say <b>Kain tayo!</b> (Let's eat!) to anyone nearby. When you can't eat more, say <b>Busog na ako.</b></p>
{{ex:Kumain ka na?|koo-MAH-een kah nah|Have you eaten? (to a friend)}}
{{ex:Kumain na po kayo?|koo-MAH-een nah poh kah-YOH|Have you eaten? (polite)}}
{{ex:Kain tayo!|KAH-een TAH-yoh|Let's eat!}}
{{ex:Busog na ako.|boo-SOHG nah ah-KOH|I'm full.}}
<h3>Rice and ulam</h3>
<p>A meal is <b>kanin</b> (cooked rice) plus <b>ulam</b>, the dish you eat with it: adobo, sinigang, fish, vegetables. English has no word for ulam; "What's for dinner?" is often <i>Ano ang ulam?</i></p>
<h3>Ordering: number + linker + dish + po</h3>
<p>At a carinderia (a small eatery) or a restaurant, say the number, the linker, the dish, and <b>po</b> to the staff. <b>nga</b> softens the order, like "please". "One more" is <b>isa pa</b>, and before a noun the linker moves onto <b>pa</b>: <b>isa pang kanin</b>.</p>
{{ex:Isang adobo nga po.|ee-SAHNG ah-DOH-boh ngah pohq|One adobo, please.}}
{{ex:Dalawang kanin po.|dah-lah-WAHNG KAH-neen pohq|Two orders of rice, please.}}
{{ex:Isa pang kanin po.|ee-SAH pahng KAH-neen pohq|One more rice, please.}}
<h3>At the sari-sari store</h3>
<p>The sari-sari store is the little neighborhood shop. Call out <b>Pabili po!</b> ("I'd like to buy, please!"), then say what you want with <b>ng</b>.</p>
{{ex:Pabili po ng tinapay.|pah-bee-LEE poh nahng tee-NAH-pai|Some bread, please.}}
<h3>Prices</h3>
<p>Ask <b>Magkano po?</b> or, for the whole bill, <b>Magkano po lahat?</b> Up to about a hundred, prices are usually said with Spanish numbers (<b>bente pesos</b>, <b>singkwenta pesos</b>); native numbers (<b>dalawampung piso</b>) are correct too. From a hundred up, native numbers are normal: <b>isang daan</b>, <b>limang daan</b>.</p>
{{ex:Magkano po lahat?|mahg-KAH-noh poh lah-HAHT|How much is it all?}}
{{ex:Bente pesos po.|BEHN-teh PEH-sohs pohq|Twenty pesos.}}
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> ordering the English way, with no linker and no po. <i>Isa adobo</i> → <b>Isang adobo po</b>.</div>
`,
